  (text "RS-485: MAX3485 (3.3 V version of the MAX485) run from +3V3, so RO feeds GP9 with no level shifting.\nDE and /RE tied to GP10: HIGH = transmit, LOW = listen. The 10k PULLDOWN sets the safe default --\nthe breakout module pulls them UP, so it drives the bus while the Pico's GPIO is still floating at boot.\nBias 270R/270R holds the idle bus at ~330 mV differential (>200 mV, so RO is defined when nobody drives).\nFit the 120R terminator ONLY at the two physical ends of the bus.\nA/B leave on J1-14/15 (twist them) with a dedicated ground return on J1-9 -- separate wire from the pin-2\npower ground, so the ceiling lamp's 0.8 A return does not move the RS-485 reference." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 415 165 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e884275b-df65-4f7d-b03f-f65e4ed14461"))
  (wire (pts (xy 330.2 299.72) (xy 330.2 303.53)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "9e5289a0-59e6-4b45-842e-93353e4b8e94"))
